<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s220S">Here is the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w1">second point</span> [of still another discussion]. One may ask the following: Those who <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w4">believe</span> that <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w2">entities</span> have <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w3"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s220m2">no</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s220m1">natural existence</span></span> [meaning the Madhyamika Prasangika (or Consequence) School] <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w7">do not accept</span> the concepts of a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w5">foundation consciousness</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w6">and the like</span>; <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w9">how then</span> is it that they can still assert that <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s220p1">all the workings of karma and its consequences</span> are totally <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s220w8">right and proper</span>?</span>
